            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to seize up, then the Telugu for to get blocked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పార్కింగు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పార్కింగు — pārkiṅgu — \"parking\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ దుకాణం దగ్గర పార్కింగు లేదు. ā dukāṇaṁ daggara pārkiṅgu lēdu. There is no parking near that shop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A parking place is పార్కింగు (pārkiṅgu) స్థలం."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పార్కింగు (pārkiṅgu) is a loan from English parking, with the Telugu final -ఉ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
