          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిలుపు — nilupu — \"to pull up; to park\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అతను కారును చెట్టు కింద నిలిపాడు. atanu kārunu ceṭṭu kinda nilipāḍu. He parked the car under a tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): నిలిపాను, nilipānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The causative of నిలుచు, to stand: to make something stand. It also means to stop a process."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిలుపు (nilupu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3675 lists Telugu nilupu, \"to cause to stand, to stop\", beside nilucu, \"to stand\"."
            }
          ]
